I posted the same gripe during my recent monk ascension.  I, too,
thought this was annoying.  I feel that all monks, not just weaponless
ones, should never get weapons from their deity.  I don't believe that
gifting of weapons should depend on your conduct, however, as nothing
else seems to.  Conducts are really just a way of challenging yourself
within the game.
 
> 2) Wielding Pick-axes and dig a wall break this conduct?  You must use 
> digging wands? this must be a problem in the gnomish cellar.

No, this does not break the conduct.  Nor, do I believe, does swinging
any weapon at a monster and missing.  IIRC, the "weaponless" conduct
is really "You never hit with a wielded weapon."  Note, this
explicitly allows you to use missile weapons (although smacking a
monster with your bow/crossbow will break conduct).  A stack of +7
silver daggers in your quiver would not break the conduct, although I
refused such a conduct, as I wanted a true "weaponless" character
(neglecting that my 'fists of death' were quite the 'weapon'!)...  Oh,
and wielding a cockatrice corpse also does not break conduct.  It's
how I cleared the treasure zoo in the middle of Rodney's tower.
 
